{"schema_version":"baseline-1.0","run_kind":"single_agent_baseline","sequence":2,"event_id":"evt-5094e023-29a4-41fa-b5a0-9ca0a527c174","run_id":"baseline-805e18f3-64e7-4ea2-8235-6b7139f22fa4","actor":{"kind":"runtime"},"occurred_at":"2026-11-01T22:37:26.625881700+00:00","prev_hash":"73ede4d2f326aa0af9fd02e91f45ef8ac6f2323bf8deb3af316f7ec91d116d1f","hash":"7b74f467966bb29261a556fe48298fce26ecbbed0fca045d4beb9653ca2f7446","payload":{"type":"recall_planned","plan":{"source":{"kind":"consensus_log","log_sha256":"faaf46b9e506f90f53217ef9eac189f68b13af7ffe4c9afe81bc3e8a23fad6ee","run_id":"run-aa966e9f-db00-455d-bc04-8f714d8839ad"},"queries":["This proposal does not increase retry attempts, expand retryable operations, or change retry backoff relative to the existing documented retry constraints.","This proposal adds no retries for payment requests; mitigation is limited to connection-pool/keep-alive configuration and explicit connect/read timeout configuration.","Any retry occurring after this change will follow the pre-existing documented retry-eligibility rules, including any documented idempotency requirement.","The revised configuration sets the payment-client RetryPolicy to max_attempts=3 and jitter_ms=50, replacing the default max_attempts=1 and jitter_ms=0 and staying within the documented cap of 3 attempts with at least 50 ms jitter.","send_with_retries will retry only SendError::Timeout up to RetryPolicy.max_attempts; upstream errors will be returned at once without a retry.","Verification will run constraint_cap_is_three_attempts, which fails when max_attempts is above 3 or jitter_ms equals 0.","constraint_cap_is_three_attempts fails when max_attempts is above 3 or jitter_ms equals 0; it does not by itself enforce the documented minimum of 50 ms, so verification will separately assert that the configured jitter_ms is at least 50."],"limit_per_query":5,"max_records":20}}}
